A||||15||wardog85GT||Car seems to stumble at cruising speed....what gives?||||5||
Z||000000||wardog85GT||07-15-2001||10:06 PM||||I have an 85 GT and it seems to want to stumble when I am at a steady speed. I dont get the stumble while accelerating and when I feel it acting up I just give it more throttle and the problem stops. Can anyone help me?||||reg||5
Z||000001||anthony_86gt||07-15-2001||11:01 PM||||I have an 86 gt and i have the same problem.  so if you find out let me know too.||||reg||4
Z||000002||Fiero_24||07-16-2001||12:03 AM||||Well it is not really an answer but something that happened to me.  I have the same stumble, so I took it to WI this weekend to give it a really good tune up, Wires, plugs, coil, fuel filter, dis cap and rotor, air filter, and oil change.  On my way home I noticed the same stumbel and next thing you know, BANG!  The car died.  So I started it up and drove some more, and then BANG again.  Turns out the cat is cloged and when it heats up it messes the air flow up.  I was told the engine will then make it run rich.  Don't know if this helps, but this is what happened to me.  Don't let it ;eave you on the highway like mine did.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||8
Z||000003||Ken Wittlief||07-16-2001||09:26 AM||||Teh cat on my daughters saturn clogged up recently - it was easy to debug - the engine roared and sputters on hard acceleration<P>  but the dead give away - at idle there was almost NO exhaust coming out the tail pipe.<P>  if your car is accelerating ok but acts funny at a steady speed i would suspect the EGR is messed up - either you plugged it, or its not opening up when the ECM tells it to<P>  cause when the ECM tells the EGR to open (almost always when you are crusing at a steady speed) it adjusts the timing to compensate - if everything is working correctly you dont feel anything - but if the EGR is not right the car will feel like its surging - speeding up and slowing down a little all by itself.||||reg||10
Z||000004||k2m4||07-16-2001||10:47 AM||||Any one think it may be a messed up TCC, not properly kicking in?? Just a thought ||||reg||5
Z||000005||k2m4||07-16-2001||10:48 AM||||Or vacume leak possibly??||||reg||5
Z||000006||Fiero_24||07-16-2001||12:00 PM||||I just added a brand new EGR to mine along with a new EGR tube too.  My cat is the problem on mine.  You can hear it rattling at idle speeds, and if you hit it you can hear the insides rolling around.  I can drive for 40 minutes, but after that it heats up so much that it chokes the motor off with a big A$$ bang.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||4
Z||000007||Tweek||07-16-2001||01:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by k2m4:<BR><B>Any one think it may be a messed up TCC, not properly kicking in?? Just a thought </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes I had that happen to me.. took a little while to figure out. At cruising speed only It would buck every couple of seconds.. I unplugged it and the problem went away.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||terryk||07-16-2001||02:32 PM||||Just lightly press the brake while holding the throttle steady. If the problem goes away, it's the TCC chattering. In out in out.||||reg||1
Z||000009||86SE||07-16-2001||03:38 PM||||Try unplugging the tach filter (its on a small white connector around under the EGR valve).  It fixed my problem, you just wont have a tach, but if its not the problem, plug it back in.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://fierodude.hypermart.net/mysig.jpg"> <BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero -- 3.4L Conversion *SUSPENDED* --<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||1
Z||000010||k2m4||07-16-2001||04:02 PM||||yeah when my TCC gave me trouble it only did it when i was on the highway cruising at a steady speed...it felt like bucking stumbling sensation kind of annoying. i really dont remember what i did to fix it(thats was 3 fieros ago) <BR>But that may be a  problem or your problem.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Ronen||07-16-2001||05:57 PM||||Its your LTC on your GM THM 125 L.U. Transmission. I had the exact same problem. It is probably sticky at this time Fieros are famous for this problem.||||reg||1
Z||000012||wardog85GT||07-16-2001||09:49 PM||||Whats the TCC?||||reg||12
Z||000013||terryk||07-16-2001||11:05 PM||||Torque Converter Clutch. They get dirt in them and hang up. Usually on, which makes for a interesting stop.||||reg||1
Z||000014||wardog85GT||07-17-2001||10:52 PM||||My car is a 4 speed std.||||reg||1
Z||000015||kempo||07-18-2001||12:11 AM||||I have an 87 GT same problem.  Actually, the problem occurred after I put in AC Delco Spark Plugs in place of the pre-existing BOSCH plugs that were in it.  After I got it to pass emissions, I put the old bosch plugs back in and it didn't do it anymore.  Check your plugs - cheap fix.  Good Luck.||||reg||1
